<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Paskevich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1782–1856</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ivan Fyodorovich Paskevich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Paskevich was a Russian field marshal who won the wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 1826–1828 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in 1828–1829. He captured Erivan in 1827, for which he was named Count of Erivan, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a> gave the khanate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In 1831 he crushed the Polish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/november-uprising">November Uprising</a> and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, then governed Congress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-paskevich.jpg" alt="Ivan Paskevich" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Dawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%98%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%A4%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87_%D0%9F%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
